# nr-office-com-transport: the new crate mixdog-office-com (Microsoft Office COM transport). Applied by the wave's wiring.

## native/core/Cargo.toml
[workspace] members, after "crates/mixdog-exthost":
    "crates/mixdog-office-com",
[workspace.dependencies] "Internal crates", after the `mixdog-exthost = ...` line:
    mixdog-office-com = { path = "crates/mixdog-office-com" }

## native/core/Cargo.lock
New package entry (the build is --locked: regenerate offline with `cargo metadata --offline --manifest-path native/core/Cargo.toml`
after the two lines above; the edges are):
    name = "mixdog-office-com", version = "1.5.0"
    dependencies = ["mixdog-fsio", "mixdog-office-com", "mixdog-rt", "mixdog-testkit", "mixdog-workspace-hack", "serde_json", "sha2 0.10.9", "tokio", "tokio-util"]
Every crate named is already in the lock (nothing is added from the registry). The `mixdog-office-com` edge is the crate's own
dev-dependency with feature `test-support` (the same shape as mixdog-exthost).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml
No new crate. Regenerate the hakari section (`cargo hakari generate`) if the lead's flow does so for a new member: the new crate
uses tokio features rt, process, io-util, macros, sync, time (and rt-multi-thread, test-util-free, in its tests).

## The consumer (a later task, not this one)
The crate registers no protocol method and no service; nothing is added to SERVICE_PENDING by this task. Whoever composes it
(the Office tool service of the track) does, once at start:
    let office = mixdog_office_com::OfficeCom::new(mixdog_office_com::OfficeComConfig::new(data_dir, tokens));
with `data_dir` the Mixdog data directory (the scripts land in <data_dir>/office/com/<16 hex>/) and `tokens` the process's LaneTokens
(`maintenance_io` writes the scripts, `spawn_io` starts the hosts), keeps it for the process and calls
    office.shutdown().await
where Node's process-exit hook and src/ext-host/methods.mjs closeOfficeSessions ran: the ext-host worker's end (Engine::shutdown),
so every session host gets its EOF cleanup and the call returns once each host is gone or its 15 s drain grace lapsed.
API for that task: OfficeCom::{detect, call, open_session, close_session, session_identity, shutdown, supported}; answers are
serde_json::Value in the shape Node's com-adapter returned; OfficeReply.host_exit is the one-shot `hostExit` signal (callers that own
files the host holds open await HostExit::wait).

